{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he left his garment in her hand</b> — Out of respect for his mistress, he did not want to snatch it from her hand by force, since he was much stronger than her. Rather, he slipped it off himself, for it was a garment he wrapped himself in, like a cloak or turban. When she saw that he had left his garment in her hand, she feared lest he expose her to the people of the household or to his master, so she preempted them by saying that he had stripped off his garment in order to lie with her. And when she saw — as she said, \"I raised my voice\" — that he fled in panic. This is the reason for \"and it came to pass, when she saw that he had left his garment\": she therefore did not say herself, \"and he left his garment in my hand,\" but rather said to the men of her household and to her husband, \"and he left his garment beside me.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:42:02.684247722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}